<title>UK: Crown Leisure shares set debut premium. [CORRECTED 18:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>Crown Leisure shares set debut premium. [CORRECTED 18:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British amusement machine supplier Crown Leisure Plc rose to a premium in modest trading as they made their debut on the London Stock Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 80-1/2p (corrects) with 173,942 shares traded by 1525 GMT, after being placed by brokerage Butterfield Securities at 77p.</p>
<p>Crown raised 7.5 million stg (corrects) in the placing, of which 2.5 million went to Natwest Ventures who were exiting their investment.</p>
<p>- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
